.TH PHYLLO-INIT 1 "Phyllotaxis" "phyllo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phyllo-init \- create minimal declarative project configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phyllo init
.RB [ --profile
.BR utility | editorial ]
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RB [ --format
.BR text | json ]
.RB [ --quiet ]
.RB [ --no-color ]
.br
.B phyllo init --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phyllo init
discovers the nearest project root containing package.json and proposes or
creates only phyllotaxis.json. The default configuration selects the generic
adapter; the optional semantic profile is utility or editorial.
Initialization refuses to overwrite an existing configuration and never
installs packages or runs project scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --profile utility|editorial
Select an accepted semantic Chroma profile in the generated configuration.
Omitting this option leaves the profile unspecified.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Preview the exact proposed configuration without writing a file.
.TP
.B --format text|json
Select human-readable text or the versioned JSON result. Text is the default.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress non-error human success and informational output. It does not alter
machine output, mutation semantics, or exit status.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI color in human output. This is also implied by non-TTY output, NO_COLOR, or TERM=dumb.
.TP
.B --help
Display command help without discovering a project.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Configuration was created or its dry-run preview completed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage, missing project root, or pre-existing configuration.
.TP
.B 3
Operational failure prevented creating the configuration.
.TP
.B 4
Unexpected internal CLI failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT where the platform/runtime uses conventional signal propagation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B phyllotaxis.json
Only file created by this command; exclusive creation prevents overwrite.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phyllo (1),
.BR phyllo-status (1)
